WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.400
-Thank you for being here.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.334
You were trending
on Twitter recently, and --

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:06.801
You know what I'm talking about?

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:08.033
-I do, only because --

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:09.734
I mean, if --
when that happens to you,

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:11.467
I feel like it happens to you
more than it happens to me,

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:12.734
but when it happened to me,

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:15.501
I felt like I must have done
something terrible.

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:16.968
-Yeah.
-I immediately reverted

00:00:16.968 --> 00:00:18.701
to a 5-year-old, like,
"What did I do?"

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:20.667
-"What'd I do?"
Yeah, "What did I do?"

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:21.868
-"What did they find out?"

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:23.367
-Yeah, "I know It didn't die."

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:25.267
-Yeah, exactly.
I'm still here, so that's good.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:26.367
-Okay, yeah.
-That's good.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:30.334
-Yeah.
So what was your take on this?

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:33.501
-Well, my take was,
try to put on the cool face.

00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:35.601
"Oh, really? That --
For -- For -- Why?"

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:36.968
-Who let you know?
Who let you know

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:38.000
that you're trending?

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.434
-It was one of the grips
on set.

00:00:39.434 --> 00:00:41.133
He's like, "Hey, man,
you're trending on Twitter,"

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:43.234
and then he went off to do
his thing, and I was like...

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:44.334
-"My career is over."
-..."I'll be right back."

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:46.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:48.767
-But you were trending because
of a very specific scene

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:50.234
that you shot
on "Dawson's Creek"...

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:51.367
-Yeah.
-...many years ago.

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:54.734
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.734 --> 00:00:57.267
All right.
-Someone tweeted about it

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:59.300
and was very confused.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.033
We actually have the clip.
Let's take a look.

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:04.234
-I said check it, Oompa-Loompa.
God...

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:05.868
Hey, ladies, I really love
what you did

00:01:05.868 --> 00:01:06.901
with that last cheer.

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:08.767
-Ohh!
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:10.200
Oh! [ Laughs ]
-I mean...

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:16.701
So, now...

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:18.434
-Damn.
-Does the ball hit the camera

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:19.601
after it hit your face?

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.634
-The ball hit the camera
after it hit my face,

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:23.501
and they loved it so much
that they --

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:25.434
I think we did two or three
more takes, is my recollection.

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:27.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:28.734
Somebody had some issues they
were trying to work out with me.

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:30.000
-Now, was it
supposed to do that?

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.934
-Never supposed to do that.
And then here's --

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:34.634
So, you know,
Twitter has its ups and downs,

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.000
but one of the things
I love about Twitter

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.367
is, man, people get into it.

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:38.868
So when I did finally
get back to my trailer,

00:01:38.868 --> 00:01:41.400
I realized I hadn't screwed up
and I wasn't dead,

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.067
my career wasn't over --
all good things,

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:48.534
there's like a forensic analysis
of this 25-year-old TV show.

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:49.767
"It was CG."

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:51.467
Someone's going frame by frame,

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:53.567
"Well, you can see he dodged
the ball at the wrong time,

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:55.267
so the ball's not --"

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.801
This was just a beach ball

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:58.100
painted to look like
a basketball

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.667
that got bounced off my face.
-That's...

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:03.534
There you go.
That's the trick.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:05.467
So it didn't hurt.

00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:06.801
-I mean, it didn't feel great.

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:08.100
-It didn't feel great, yeah.
-It's not amazing.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.067
-After three takes, like,
"I think we got it, right?"

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:11.934
-And, also, I'm like 19,
so, you know, you're like,

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:14.701
[ Voice breaking ] "I'm fine.
Everything's cool.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.501
Throw it harder, man."
-"Harder.

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:18.400
Use a real basketball
this time, man."

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.033
Yeah. You also broke
the Internet again

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:23.834
during this past Halloween.

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:26.667
You were photographed
going to a Halloween party

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:29.100
dressed as Charlie Conway
from "Mighty Ducks."

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.501
This is your character.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:34.467
Your character.

00:02:34.467 --> 00:02:37.200
Do you keep a Charlie Conway
jersey in your closet?

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.200
-Actually, this is my lovely
wife's Charlie Conway jersey

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.834
that she keeps in her closet

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:43.868
for occasions such as this.
-But I love that she --

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:46.033
'Cause she always -- she kind of
does this on purpose.

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:47.901
She wears Pacey T-shirts
and stuff.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.300
-Yeah, well, there's
a notorious Pacey T-shirt,

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.734
as well, that she has.

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:57.000
That is my face in Ray-Bans
that she cut into a crop top.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.734
And I'm shooting
in Wilmington right now,

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:02.667
and the first day I was working
when she got in

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:04.133
and I come back home,
and she's like,

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:05.667
"Don't worry. I'm just
at Target, grabbing some stuff."

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:09.501
And I come home, and she's her
in the crop top Pacey shirt.

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:11.767
And I'm like, "Babe,
you can't wear that here."

00:03:11.767 --> 00:03:13.868
[ Laughter ]
"Like, not here."

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:15.968
-Yeah, there.
She can do whatever she wants.

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:17.734
Did people freak
when they saw the costume?

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:19.868
-Yeah, the -- Well, this is
super name-dropping,

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:22.133
but I found out something
very important.

00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:24.601
Margot Robbie,
big "Mighty Ducks" fan.

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:26.767
-Wow!
-She was at that party,

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:28.434
and she was like --
she turned around,

00:03:28.434 --> 00:03:30.067
and for the -- the first thing
she saw was the jersey.

00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:31.300
She's like, "Oh, my God!
I love that movie."

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.734
And then she looked up
and was like,

00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:33.834
"Oh, I get it."

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:35.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.501 --> 00:03:37.133
-"Really good costume.
Really good.

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:38.300
That's really cool."

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.033
I want to talk about
"Fatal Attraction."

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:41.567
-Yes, please.
-That's a big deal, buddy.

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:44.167
This is the TV adaptation
of the hit movie,

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:46.667
but this is told in a
different way than the movie.

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:48.067
-A different way
and a different time.

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:51.167
So, the movie is made
and set in 1987.

00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:56.934
Our TV show is is made in 2023
and set in 2008 and 2023,

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.767
which mostly gives us
the opportunity --

00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:01.367
Well, one, it's TV, right?
So we have more time.

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:05.133
And if you watch the original
movie, it's an amazing film,

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:07.267
but the culture
has moved, right?

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:08.734
There's just some things

00:04:08.734 --> 00:04:10.501
that you couldn't get away
with now even if you tried.

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:12.968
So we have the opportunity
to really delve

00:04:12.968 --> 00:04:15.968
into this iconic character
of Alex Forrest

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:18.634
and explain a little bit
of, like, why she is

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:21.300
and what made her
into the woman that she is.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:24.133
And then, on the Dan side,
my character's side,

00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:25.501
we have an opportunity
to show, like,

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:27.434
you know, there are consequences
to your actions.

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:28.767
[ Chuckles ]
-Yeah.

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:30.901
You were telling me backstage
that you ran into someone

00:04:30.901 --> 00:04:33.067
recently who
was a big fan of how

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:34.868
the "Fatal Attraction" series
turned out.

00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:37.000
I know you don't want
to name-drop, but...

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.601
-No, I totally
want to name-drop.

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:39.767
-Okay, good.
-I totally --

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:41.400
I'm so happy you brought this up
because I want

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.767
everybody on the planet
to know this story.

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:45.534
-Good.
-So...

00:04:45.534 --> 00:04:47.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.767
And it starts name-dropping,
and it only gets worse.

00:04:48.767 --> 00:04:52.067
So, I was at the Vanity Fair
Oscar afterparty.

00:04:52.067 --> 00:04:55.234
-Yeah. All right.
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:04:55.234 --> 00:04:56.534
-That's fine.
A lot of people go to that.

00:04:56.534 --> 00:04:58.334
-I was having a --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.334 --> 00:04:59.634
I was having a conversation

00:04:59.634 --> 00:05:02.701
with multi-Oscar nominee
and winner Michelle Williams,

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:04.434
an old friend of mine.
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:05:04.434 --> 00:05:06.734
-Now we're --
Now we're talking.

00:05:06.734 --> 00:05:08.033
-And in the middle
of my conversation,

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:09.467
a woman who works at Paramount+

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:11.133
who is putting on
"Fatal Attraction,"

00:05:11.133 --> 00:05:12.534
came up and said,
"You know, the show is great.

00:05:12.534 --> 00:05:15.367
Congratulations.
And Steven...

00:05:15.367 --> 00:05:18.367
Spielberg..."
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:05:18.367 --> 00:05:19.667
...who is the producer
of the movie,

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:20.934
"loves it, and congratulations."

00:05:20.934 --> 00:05:21.968
And I was like,
"Oh, that's great.

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:23.934
Oh, my God, amazing.
Can't wait."

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:25.601
And then that conversation ends,

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:28.701
and Steven Spielberg
walks across the room

00:05:28.701 --> 00:05:31.567
and comes up to me and says,
"Joshua..."

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:34.300
knows my first name.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.934
"...you are amazing
in this show.

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:38.367
You're great. I loved it.
You and Lizzy, you're fantastic.

00:05:38.367 --> 00:05:41.033
Your chemistry's incredible."
And he goes on --

00:05:41.033 --> 00:05:42.567
I have no idea
how long it was for

00:05:42.567 --> 00:05:43.934
because I had
an out-of-body experience.

00:05:43.934 --> 00:05:46.501
I didn't really hear
much of what he said.

00:05:46.501 --> 00:05:48.234
Then he finishes,
he walks away,

00:05:48.234 --> 00:05:49.801
and I had this
terrible moment of, like,

00:05:49.801 --> 00:05:51.100
"Oh, my God.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.334
I hope somebody
that I know witnessed that

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:56.033
because nobody's
ever going to believe that."

00:05:56.033 --> 00:05:57.334
-No, of course.
-And it turns out my friend Doug

00:05:57.334 --> 00:05:59.067
was standing right there,
and he saw my face and went,

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:01.701
"Yeah, yeah, I saw it."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.701 --> 00:06:04.400
And now you all know.
And now we all know.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:06.467
And Doug.
-And Doug.

00:06:06.467 --> 00:06:08.133
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:11.501
Here's Steven Spielberg's
favorite production,

00:06:11.501 --> 00:06:13.734
Joshua Jackson
in "Fatal Attraction."

00:06:13.734 --> 00:06:15.334
Take a look at this.

00:06:17.367 --> 00:06:19.467
-Idiots.
-I agree.

00:06:19.467 --> 00:06:22.434
-I do.
Hi.

00:06:22.434 --> 00:06:24.734
-Hi.
-This is Alex...

00:06:24.734 --> 00:06:26.634
I forgot your last name.

00:06:26.634 --> 00:06:27.801
-Forrest.
-Alex Forrest.

00:06:27.801 --> 00:06:30.200
My husband, Dan.
Dan, Alex Forrest.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.400
-No, I know him already.
-Oh.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.567
-From, uh, the criminal courts.

00:06:35.567 --> 00:06:38.334
I work in Victim Services.
-Oh.

00:06:38.334 --> 00:06:40.934
-That's with Conchita, right?
-Right.

00:06:40.934 --> 00:06:42.367
-Wow!
Are you kidding?

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:43.501
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:43.501 --> 00:06:44.701
-You were right, Beth.

00:06:44.701 --> 00:06:47.767
This place --
I mean, it's -- it's magical.

00:06:47.767 --> 00:06:51.200
-Well...
We've been very happy here.

00:06:53.234 --> 00:06:55.100
-I can feel it.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.701
The happiness.

00:06:58.667 --> 00:07:01.701
-Eee!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:01.701 --> 00:07:04.033
Joshua Jackson, everybody!

00:07:04.033 --> 00:07:08.200
"Fatal Attraction"
comes to Paramount+ on Sunday.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:10.834
We'll be right back with
stand-up from Jackie Fabulous.

00:07:10.834 --> 00:07:12.501
Come on back.

